# synthesized expect_contains entry can be pinned to a string the tool really
# prints. v1 only ran the script with --help in a temp dir: that captured
# argparse noise and never the verdict/report lines the tools build with
# out.append/format_report, so the teacher invented plausible literals
# ("No violations", "2 violations", "no conflict found") that no tool emits and
# four clean-case tests failed against skills that worked.
