# path): capture_phrase_pool reached real tool vocabulary only when someone
# hand-built a pool file and pointed SKILL_HISTORY_POOL at it, so the default
# teacher pool was static vocabulary alone and expected literals were optimized
# against strings the tool never prints (scratch/skill-compiler-realharvest-
# 2026-10-01/FINDING.md). The history live-run pool is now harvested by default
# from the mind trajectory: the stdout half of (cmd, stdout) pairs whose command
# actually executes the skill's own script. Line acceptance is by OUTPUT SHAPE,
# not command text, per the contamination rule in RECLASSIFY.md: a line is kept
# when it looks like report text and is not a verbatim line of the skill's own
# source, which is the class that put 29 Python source lines in the counterpoint
# pool. Cache at $SKILL_HARVEST_CACHE/pool-history-<skill>.json with a TTL
# (SKILL_HARVEST_TTL, default 3600s; SKILL_HARVEST_REFRESH=1 forces a rebuild).
# SKILL_HISTORY_POOL still wins when set, SKILL_AUTO_HARVEST=0 turns this off.
harvest_history_pool() {
    local skill_abs="${1:-}"
